   "content": "<h3>Examination number : ______</h3>\n<h3>Tsapa Primary School</h3>\n<p><strong>2018 – 2019 END OF TERM TWO EXAMINATIONS FOR STANDARD 5</strong></p>\n<h3>Primary Science</h3>\n<p>( 100 marks)</p>\n<p>Name of candidate : ______ Date : ______</p>\n<h3>Instructions :</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Write your name on each paper</li>\n<li>Cheating is not allowed if found you will be penalized</li>\n<li>Write your number on each page</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"unit1\">Section A: 2Omarks</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>The growing of trees is called ___</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>Poultry</li>\n<li>Silviculture</li>\n<li>Agronomy</li>\n<li>Floriculture</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>The following are the major elements of agricultural ______</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>Commercial and poultry</li>\n<li>Commercial and subsistence</li>\n<li>Subsistence and agronomy</li>\n<li>Agronomy and poultry</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>The following are the major elements of agricultural environment</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>Soil, water and plants</li>\n<li>Wind and glass</li>\n<li>Glass and wood</li>\n<li>Animals and manure</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>The farm tool above is called</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>Rake</li>\n<li>Sickle</li>\n<li>Watering can</li>\n<li>Panga knife</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>What is the farm tool used for?</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>Lifting seedlings</li>\n<li>Watering seedlings</li>\n<li>Cutting maize stalks</li>\n<li>Clearing land</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>Crops grown mainly for sale are</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>Food crops</li>\n<li>Agronomy</li>\n<li>Cash crops</li>\n<li>Cassava</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>Main is grown in ______</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>Dedza and Ntcheu</li>\n<li>Kasungu</li>\n<li>All districts in malawi</li>\n<li>Mwanza and salima</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>Some of the diseases of maize are _____.</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>Leaf bright and head smut</li>\n<li>Star grass</li>\n<li>Maize weevil</li>\n<li>Army worm</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>Identify the farm animal above</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>Pigeon</li>\n<li>Turkey</li>\n<li>Duck</li>\n<li>Pig</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>The growing of crops and rearing animals is called ______</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>Agronomy</li>\n<li>Silviculture</li>\n<li>Agriculture</li>\n<li>Poultry</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>Which of the following is the correct meaning of the term energy</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>Ability to do work</li>\n<li>Study of things</li>\n<li>Things around us</li>\n<li>Ability to walk</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>Which of the following is the correct type of energy.</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>Hot energy</li>\n<li>Chemical energy</li>\n<li>Bulb energy</li>\n<li>Battery</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>What one activity can you do to produce heat energy</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>Scratching</li>\n<li>Burning wood</li>\n<li>Walking on the sun</li>\n<li>Eating food</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>What is the use of electrical energy</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>Photosynthesis</li>\n<li>Cooking</li>\n<li>Blowing a whistle</li>\n<li>Bending a wire</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>Which of the following define the term production</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>Making things</li>\n<li>Selling things</li>\n<li>Buying things</li>\n<li>Getting customers</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>What are the marketing technologies necessary for increasing sales and profit</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>Advertising</li>\n<li>Selling</li>\n<li>Television</li>\n<li>Buying</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>Why are marketing technologies importance?</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>Advertising</li>\n<li>Telephone messages</li>\n<li>Outdoor messages</li>\n<li>Decreasing sales</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>What is an environment</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>Surrounding in which plants and animals live</li>\n<li>Surrounding in which people live</li>\n<li>Surroundings in which plants live</li>\n<li>Surrounding in which people and wild animals live</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>The following are major food nutrients except</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>Vegetables</li>\n<li>Vitamins</li>\n<li>Fats and oil</li>\n<li>Water</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>Give one function of vitamins</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>Promoting growth</li>\n<li>Repair worn out body tissues</li>\n<li>Making bone strong</li>\n<li>Farming red blood</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"unit2\">Section B</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Define weeding?</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>Why is weeding important</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>Mention three common weeds in Malawi</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>What is the difference between cash and food crops?</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>Mention four pests of maize</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>List three methods of weeding</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>What is crop husbandry practice</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>Give four importance of crops</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>Mention three crops grown in Malawi?</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>List three common tools that you know</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Science</h3>\n<p><em><strong>Study the figure above and answer the question that follows</strong></em></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Name the marketing technology</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Shown above</p>\n<ol>\n<li>State one importance of marketing technology shown above.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><em><strong>Study the food chain below and answer the questions that follows.</strong></em></p>\n<ol>\n<li>What would happen if there were no green plants in the food chain?</li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n<li>What would happen to the chicken if there no grasshopper</li>\n</ol>\n<p>13. Why is good nutrition important to the body?</p>\n<p>14. Explain two functions of proteins?</p>\n<p>15. What do you understand by the term malnutrition?</p>\n<p>16. Write down food chain involving plants and animals around the school</p>\n<h3>End of Question Paper</h3>"
